3. Nc3 { [%cal Gc3d5,Gc3e4] } (3. Nf3 { Ends up in the same position. } 3... Nf6 4. Nc3) 3... Nf6 { [%cal Gf6d5,Gf6e4] } 4. Nf3 { [%cal Gf3e5,Gf3d4] } 4... dxc4 { That's the Slav Proper. Thanks to our Pawn in c6, the sacrificed Pawn will be harder to get back. } { [%csl Gc6][%cal Gb7b5] } (4... Bf5 { Developing our Bishop right away would lead to a double attack. } 5. cxd5 cxd5 6. Qb3 { [%cal Gb3d5,Gb3b7] }) 5. a4 { Better for White to prevent b5 right away. And now we can develop our Bishop. } { [%cal Ga4b5,Gc8f5] } (5. e4 { The usual move to retrieve the Pawn can be defended and can lead to attack on the Knight. } { [%csl Gc3][%cal Gf1c4] } 5... b5 6. a4 b4) (5. e3 { Similar result with a safer move. } 5... b5 6. a4 b4) 5... Bf5 { From there we'll just have to develop our second Bishop and then castle. } { [%cal Ge7e6,Gf8b4] } *


