3. cxd5 { We can exchange Pawns, that was the whole purpose. Tends to end in symetrical positions. } 3... cxd5 4. Nc3 { [%cal Gc3d5,Gc3e4] } 4... Nf6 { [%cal Gf6e4,Gf6d5] } 5. Bf4 (5. Nf3 { Would end with similar position. } { [%cal Gf3e5,Gf3d4] } 5... Nc6 { [%cal Gc6d4,Gc6e5] } 6. Bf4 Bf5) 5... Nc6 (5... Bf5 { Developing the Bishop right away ends up with a double attack. } 6. Qb3 { [%cal Gb3d5,Gb3b7] }) 6. Nf3 (6. e3 { White could also close the door directly, we would still develop our Bishop. } 6... Bf5) 6... Bf5 *


